Looking at this problem, I need to:
1. Partition a tree into connected components
2. Ensure at least one component has exactly k vertices
3. Minimize the number of edges between different components (i.e., minimize cut edges)

The key insight is that this is equivalent to finding a connected subgraph with exactly k vertices that has the minimum number of edges connecting it to the rest of the tree.

I'll use dynamic programming on trees. For each node, I'll compute the minimum number of internal cuts needed to form a connected component of each possible size (1 to k) containing that node.

